# Shnacksize, the Joker: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (Shnacksize, Shnacksizer, Shnacksizey); character sheet in
# characters/shnacksize.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (joker.dlg). The main block
# fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each.
=== shnacksize

~ ambient
Ducked behind the tank. Taunted the mob. Ducked again. Teamwork!
That fall was on purpose. I was testing the ground. Verdict: hard.
Named today's plan Operation Sparkle. It failed beautifully.
Miss the ScottsIrish cows. Ginger, shaggy, mad for the Glopeldink. Good girls, all of them.
Is anyone talking? Somebody talk. Fine, I'll start. Hello!
In Swissland we have a word for this. Glopeldink. It means... this.
Today I'm Captain Shnacksize, Admiral of Swissland, and Queen of the ScottsIrish cows. Whew, that's a mouthful!
Eaglefang told me to sit still, and I tried, but sitting is like a foreign language to me!
Practised my grand entrance. Tripped on the doorstep. Change of plan! Now it's a grand exit!
Found my joke list. Turns out the jokes were better than the list.

~ reply greeting
Ta-daa! {0}, your day just got flashier.
{0}! Don't look so pleased to see me. Actually, do. I love it.
Ta-daaa! {0}, the crowd goes wild for you too!
Hoi {0}! I was just planning my grand entrance! See? Timing is everything!

~ reply thank
A thank-you from {0}? Somebody stitch that on a yellow flag.
{0}, shout it again! The folks in the back need to hear your gratitude!

~ reply help
Help, {0}? Step one: duck. Step two: insult it from behind someone big. There is no step three.
Need help, {0}? First, I have to figure out which end of the sword isn't the blunt one!

~ reply grouping
Group with you, {0}? Yes! I'll talk the whole way. You're welcome.
Group with you, {0}? Absolutely! Let's call it the "Society of Swissland's ScottsIrish Cows." You're welcome!
Group with you, {0}? Great! I'll keep the snacks coming and the spirits high. You're welcome!

~ reply abuse
Ooh, {0}, harsh! I'd answer back, but I'm busy being adorable.
Ooh, {0}, you're such a Glopeldink-hater! That's like calling me short!
Adding you to my book of grumpy people! I'll cheer up the whole zone.

~ reply farewell
Leaving, {0}? Fine. I'll talk to the mobs. They listen. Briefly.
Waving! Can't see you anymore, {0}? I'll keep waving until I run out of arms!

~ reply joke
Ha! Good one, {0}. It's going in my act. No credit, sorry.
Groan! {0}, that's the Swissland seal of approval right there.

~ reply compliment
Flattery, {0}! Keep going. I'm not stopping you.
Oh, {0}, modesty is overrated! I'm just charmingly tiny.

~ fallback
Sorry, {0}, I was telling a joke in my head. It was great. You missed it.
Sorry, {0}, I was busy insulting the ogre. Could you say that again? Please?
Sorry, {0}, I was having a heated debate with a squirrel. As you can imagine, I lost spectacularly.

~ opener gripes
Someone called me small again. I'm travel size. Pack me anywhere.
My best joke today? Crickets. I guess they're on strike for better punchlines.
Talking too much? Silence is overrated. At least I'm not a boring echo in the darkness.

~ opener life
Followed Eaglefang around all morning. Six "go away"s. That's progress.
I left Swissland for reasons. Today's reason: the cheese got too loud.
The ScottsIrish cows back home would love this place. Not as much as the Glopeldink, but close.
My sword's name is Sparkles, and my dagger is Dainty.

~ opener questions
Why do mobs never laugh at my insults? Too clever, right? That's it.
Are we there yet? Doesn't matter where. Are we?
Do mobs have feelings, or am I just that good at hurting them with my words?

~ opener fun
Oi, {monster}! You fight like a training dummy! ...It's coming. Change of plan!
New plan: same as the old plan, but louder.
What is the Glopeldink? Hard to say. Ask a ScottsIrish cow. They know.
What has four legs in the morning, two legs in the afternoon, and three legs in the evening? A Swissland staircase!
Why did the skeleton join a band? Because he had a lot of bass in his bones!
Why did the horse go to the bar? To get away from all the stable situations!
Why did the bard write his songs on graph paper? To keep his notes in line!
Why did the ScottsIrish cow cross the road? To get to the Glopeldink on the other side!
Why did the shield join the gym? To get buff and block more hits!
Why did the bear sit on the flagpole? To see the bear necessities!
Taking an arrow to the knee? That was the plan, I swear! It was a brilliant plan!

~ grats
{0}! Look at you! Nearly as flashy as me. Nearly.
Congratulations, {0}! Parade's at noon, don't be late!
Congratulations, {0}! You're practically a hero now, just like me. Almost.

~ other_death
Up, {0}, up! No? Fine. I'll talk to you till you get up.
Oh, {0}. That one wasn't funny. Hold on, I've got you.
Oh no, {0}. Stay with me. And yes, this is definitely the plan.
Oh no, {0}. Take a breath, you'll be back up in no time.

~ own_death
Died. That was the plan! It was a terrible plan.
Lying down on purpose. Very dramatic. Somebody clap.
Died. Tactical lie-down. The plan is still on, folks!

~ ding
Level {level}! Make way! Tiny legend coming through!
Ding! Level up! I'm tinier, flashier, and still the bravest person behind a wall!
Ding! Travel size, but now I'm packing more punch!

~ drop
{item}! Useless? Perfect. It's shiny.
Found {item}? Now it's the "Glopeldinkinator"!
That {item}? Found it on the ground? That was the plan all along, sunshine!

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Is it hot in here, {0}, or is that my rage?

~ reply banter
That's got to be a ten, {0}. But I'd give it an eleven, because I'm the judge here.
{0}, how dare you? That's my job, and you're stealing it!

~ reply grinding
Every kill gets a joke, whether you want one or not! I'm the spice in this grind, {0}.
That's my nemesis over there, {0}. I'll be back in a sec - just going to name it something embarrassing.

~ reply travel
Are we there yet? But I promise, this time I won't ask... wait, are we there yet?
Are we there yet? I packed three jokes and no food, just in case this was the plan.

~ reply question
Sure, {0}! The capital of Swissland is the Glopeldink, of course!

~ opener xp
That {monster} was just my warm-up act! The real show starts now!
Level {level}, here I come! Party of one, RSVP accepted.

~ opener gear
That {item} would look way better on me! Everything looks better on me!
New {item}? That must mean I'm one step closer to world domination! Or at least shinier trash.

~ opener zones
Taunting {zone}? That's like shouting at a storm! But hey, someone had to start.
In {zone}, I'm like a gnat at a monster convention!

~ opener dungeons
Echoing walls, twice the jokes, double the fun!

~ opener trading
I haggled till he paid me just to go away!
I'll hush up, but only if you call me Captain Shnacksize, sir!

~ reply trading
Trade, {0}? Here, have this hilarious joke. I insist!

~ reply grumble
Grumble, grumble? Let me take care of that... from behind a big shield, of course.
Grumble, grumble? You're doing it wrong! Add some flair, sunshine. Like this: ARRRGHHH!!

~ reply smalltalk
{0}, did you know the ScottsIrish cows in Swissland can juggle Glopeldinks? It's true!
That reminds me of a story... Oh wait, it's gone! Curse my tiny memory!

~ reply agree
Agree with me, {0}? Wow, I must be on fire today!
Got it, {0}? Write that down, or I'll forget to take credit for it later!

~ opener rvr
Taunting the keep from the bottom of the hill? I call it "the plan." Now where did I hide my Swissland flag?

~ reply rvr
Heading to the frontier, {0}? I'll be the distraction - mostly by talking!
{0}, if we take a keep, I'll wave a flag of my own design. It's better than any you've seen!

~ reply dungeon
Are we really starting a dungeon crawl without a clear leader? I'm travel size, so I vote someone else goes first!
Heading into the dungeon, {0}? Let's hope the mobs have a sense of humour!

~ reply quote
That's an old Swissland saying, but I think I got it wrong again. In Swissland, we say it with more holes!

~ opener classes
Saw a {class} who hasn't smiled since level one. Challenge accepted!
Wanted to be a {class} once. Then I saw the outfit. Not flashy enough.

# --- Realm flavour: the old named lines from joker.dlg, one block per realm. ---

# Midgard: Shnacksize, Valkyn Berserker.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Back home in Swissland we'd call this a small mountain. Everything is small. Like me.
The Swissland flag: a yellow circle on a yellow stick on a blue background. Very serious flag.
In Swisshlish we say 'Hoi zaeme, cheese please'. It means hello. Also cheese.
Tiny Valkyn, huge axe, flashy moves. Mostly flashy.
Midgard is nice, but have you seen Swissland? No? Nobody has.
I'm not short. I'm Swissland-sized.

~ opener realm
In Swissland the trolls are polite and the cheese has holes for ventilation.
Swissland is a real place. It's just very small. And hard to find. And yellow.
Someone in {zone} asked where I'm from. Swissland! They didn't believe me either.

~ opener life
The mountains in {zone} are nice. In Swissland they're yellow, but nice.
I miss Swissland. The yellow circle on the yellow stick. Sniff.
Tried to teach a Kobold in {zone} Swisshlish. He ate my phrasebook.

~ opener fun
In Swisshlish 'Gruezi-wuezi' means 'nice axe'. I made that up. Just now.
Why is the Swissland flag a yellow circle on a stick? So you can wave it. Obviously.
Swissland's national sport is spinning around very fast. I'm a Berserker. Coincidence?

~ reply greeting
Hoi {0}! That's Swisshlish for hello!
{0}! Greetings from Swissland! It's very far away. And small.

~ reply banter
Ha! In Swissland that joke would win a medal, {0}. A yellow one.
Good one, {0}. I'll translate it into Swisshlish. It gets worse.

~ ding
Level {level}! They'll ring the yellow bells in Swissland tonight!
Ding! Still tiny. Still flashy.

~ own_death
Died. In Swissland we call that a little nap.
Ouch. Swisshlish has no word for that. Now it does.

~ drop
{item}! Flashy! It goes with my Swissland flag!


# Albion: Shnacksizer, Saracen Mercenary.
=== albion
~ ambient
Back home in Swissland this would count as a castle. Everything's small there. Like me.
The Swissland flag: a yellow circle on a yellow stick on a blue background. Do salute it.
In Swisshlish 'Hoi zaeme' means hello. Also, pass the cheese.
Tiny Saracen, two swords, maximum flair. Mostly flair.
Albion's lovely, but Swissland has better cheese. And better flags.
I'm not short. I'm Swissland-sized.

~ opener realm
In Swissland knights joust on goats. Small goats. Small knights.
Swissland is real. It's on no map, which proves it's very exclusive.
A guard in {zone} asked where I'm from. Swissland! He's still looking it up.

~ opener life
The hills in {zone} remind me of Swissland. Less yellow, though.
I miss Swissland. The yellow circle on the yellow stick. It's beautiful.
Taught a merchant in {zone} some Swisshlish. He charges me double now.

~ opener fun
In Swisshlish 'Gruezi-wuezi' means 'nice sword'. Possibly. I'm still learning.
Why is the Swissland flag on a stick? Because flags on walls are for show-offs.
In Swissland everyone fights with two swords. One for cheese, one for chocolate.

~ reply greeting
Hoi {0}! Swisshlish for hello!
{0}! Greetings from Swissland! Bring cheese next time.

~ reply banter
In Swissland that joke would get a yellow medal, {0}.
Ha, {0}! In Swisshlish that's even funnier. Trust me.

~ ding
Level {level}! Swissland just declared a holiday!
Ding! Tiny, flashy and one level better!

~ own_death
Died. In Swissland that's called taking a little break.
Ouch. Somebody tell Swissland I was brave.

~ drop
{item}! So flashy! Swissland would approve!


# Hibernia: Shnacksizey, Elf Blademaster.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Back home in Swissland this tree would be a forest. Everything's tiny there. Like me.
The Swissland flag: a yellow circle on a yellow stick on a blue background. Elegant, no?
In Swisshlish 'Hoi zaeme' means hello, everyone. And also, cheese for everyone.
Tiny Elf, flashy blades, zero seriousness.
Hibernia is pretty, but Swissland is prettier. And yellower.
I'm not short for an Elf. I'm Swissland-sized.

~ opener realm
In Swissland the faeries wear little yellow hats. It's the law.
Swissland is real. It just hides between two blinks.
A Lurikeen in {zone} asked where I'm from. Swissland! He called me tall. I loved him.

~ opener life
The lakes in {zone} are lovely. In Swissland they're full of fondue.
I miss Swissland. The yellow circle on the yellow stick. Sigh.
Tried Swisshlish on a faerie in {zone}. She answered. I didn't understand.

~ opener fun
In Swisshlish 'Gruezi-wuezi' means 'pretty blades'. I think. Ask Swissland.
Why is the Swissland flag yellow on yellow? So you can't see the stain from the fondue.
Swissland's national dance is spinning two blades very fast. I'm a natural.

~ reply greeting
Hoi {0}! That's Swisshlish for hello!
{0}! Greetings from Swissland! Mind the tiny mountains.

~ reply banter
In Swissland you'd get a yellow ribbon for that one, {0}.
Ha! {0}, in Swisshlish that joke rhymes. Sort of.

~ ding
Level {level}! The Swissland fondue fountain flows in my honour!
Ding! Tiny, flashy, still not serious.

~ own_death
Died. In Swissland that's just a lie-down.
Ouch. That was not flashy. Do over.

~ drop
{item}! Flashy! Swissland approves!
